Written by hand for this project on 2026-11-19 (CC0 1.0: no rights
reserved), in KiCad 10 text (schematic version 20260306): a project file, a
root sheet holding one sheet "io" (file io.kicad_sch) with four pins, and
that sheet's file with four hierarchical labels, out of step on purpose.
Paired by name the sheet reads: A (pin and label, both input), B (label
only), C (pin input, label output), D (pin only), E (label only) and E1 (pin
only): six rows. The fixed uuids all start 5e7a1b00-0000-4000-8000-: the
root 100, the sheet 150, the pins A 151, C 152, D 153, E1 154, the sub
sheet's file 200, the labels A 201, B 202, C 203, E 204.
tests/e2e/sheet-pins.spec.ts opens it in a sch frame for sheet.pins.get,
sheet.pins.apply and sheet.pins.place. files.json lists the files the e2e
harness opens. The KiCad files carry no comment, so this file holds their
license.
